From faea419f9f4388673dd1612cb1864640e5017df3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 20:36:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/8] feat: the portal gets a frame, and the phone keeps the
 one it had

The shell becomes a two-column grid at lg and above: a sticky sidebar
carrying the mark, the client, the project switcher, the sections and the
account, next to a workspace that holds the page. The full-width header
and the document footer stop having a job and go away -- on desktop. Below
lg the tree is the phase 8 tree, class for class, so the guarantee that
cost the most last phase (the attention answer above the fold at 375x667)
holds by construction rather than by measurement.

Three things moved rather than changed. The bottom-nav threshold is now
showsBottomNav() in config, beside the constant that defines it, so phase
9 lights the bar by adding a section and touching no layout. The project
switcher is its own component, usable from the sidebar and the phone
header. The nav learned a vertical orientation instead of growing a second
component that would drift from the first -- the active-item rule is
subtle and now still lives in one place.

Two source-reading assertions in phase8-nav-availability moved with the
rule and are documented in the test. The third, the one that forbids the
word "cycle" in the shell, is untouched and is what keeps the coming
contextual rail an opaque slot.

Nothing here knows about cycle, stage, team, attention or journey.

